439:{character:player} Don't be silly, Joseph's only away temporarily. It's not like he won't come back.
440:{character:Kana Fujita} You don't know that. Even though their company isn't as big as ours, I've heard that its owner is extremely well connected, and able to offer Joseph the chance to go and record shows in places he's never been to before.
441:{character:Kana Fujita} It also appears as though Joseph and the owner go way back. He was excited by the chance to catch up with him. That reminds me... I saw Joseph going into the company owner's office the other day. He looked pretty serious... Riichi. I wonder if maybe he really has jumped ship, after all.
442:{character:player} Is... is that so...
443:{character:Wanjirou} Well, if they're friends it's certainly a possibility, woof. Woof? Why would you play that tile, {var:player_nickname}?
445:{character:Kana Fujita} Senpai! It's too late to pretend to be all confused and try to take it back. I want that! Ippatsu!
446:{character:Kana Fujita} Huh? Senpai, you gave me an extra 1,000 points. But it's your lucky day that you're here with Kana, the epitome of honesty! If it was anyone else, you'd never see them again.
447:{character:player} Oh... Thanks for the reminder. I'm sorry everyone, but I'm suddenly feeling rather unwell. I think I'll leave after this Hanchan.
448:{character:Clerk} Hello, this is what you wanted. Can you carry it yourself, or would you like us to deliver it?
449:{character:player} Thank you, but I think I'll take it. Not much of a surprise if I don't bring it myself.
450:{character:Santa} Ho-ho-ho! Merry Christmas! I hope you have a joyous eve, my friend!
451:{character:player} Thanks. Same to you.
452:{character:Santa?} How come you seem a little down? Ho-ho-ho—!
453:{character:Joseph} Long time no see! The holiday has arrived, so cheer up, friend!
454:{character:Joseph} Huh? What was that about?
455:{character:player} Checking if I'm dreaming or not.
456:{character:Joseph} Hahaha! Then shouldn't you be pinching your own face? And that was too light, anyway...
457:{character:player} Oh, in that case...
459:{character:Joseph} Ow...! You really went for it, friend...
460:{character:player} Consider it a small punishment.
461:{character:Joseph} Punishment?
462:{character:player} Just... Leave that for now. Didn't you leave One Han City? Surely you didn't come back just for Christmas?
463:{character:Joseph} What are you talking about? Where did you hear that?
464:{character:Joseph} So that's what happened. The Little Idol guessed right, it was my old friend who invited me over there. I helped him out by hosting a show after we'd caught up, but it's a huge misunderstanding to say that I was jumping ship.
465:{character:player} But you just upped and vanished for months! Who wouldn't think you'd just left?
466:{character:Joseph} I'm so sorry, my friend. I didn't mean to stay out of touch, it's just that I had a little accident while out shooting in the sea. I ended up marooned with the crew on an uninhabited island, with all our electronics ruined by the seawater!
467:{character:Joseph} We were stuck on that island for months, before finally being rescued by a passing ship. I wanted to come back here right away, but my old friend insisted that I rest a while longer. That's why I didn't make it back until now, but at least I didn't miss Christmas!
468:{character:Joseph} ...I know it might sound a little unbelievable, but I swear I'm telling the truth.
469:{character:player} No, I believe you! But I must point out the absurdity of calling such a serious situation "a little accident"...
470:{character:player} At the very least you could have called and let me know you were safe.
471:{character:Joseph} Rather than worrying you, I thought it would be better to see you in person, safe and sound, and make light of the whole matter.
472:{character:player} I suppose that makes some sense. Oh! It's getting late, Ichihime is still waiting for us. Let's go to the shrine.
473:{character:Joseph} Okay! I've got some gifts for them. Can't wait to see how happy they are!
474:{character:Joseph} Speaking of gifts, my friend, there is still the matter of yours. What would you like? For causing you to worry so long, you can pick whatever you want.
475:{character:player} That can wait. Let's discuss as we walk.
476:{character:player} So... You didn't even consider to go join that company?
477:{character:player} I heard Kana say that they're very competent, and can offer you the chance to go to those few places you have yet to visit. Weren't you excited?
478:{character:Joseph} Our accident totally turned my friend off the idea of making an adventure show, so I can't do it even if I really wanted to!
479:{character:Joseph} I prefer the boss here. No matter how reckless I can be, I'm trusted to get the job done. Even if there are some places I can't go, I like the freedom I get working under him.
480:{character:Joseph} Not to mention the fact that I've been here so many years already. I can't just up and depart like that, leaving you and all the other people I care about.
481:{character:player} ...Are we holding you back? Are our friendships the same as those treasures, forestalling you from forging ahead? Preventing you from chasing what you always dreamed of chasing?
482:{character:Joseph} ...Sorry, my friend. Hang on one second while I light a cigarette, please.
483:{character:Joseph} Although I said I had to give up cumbersome memories in order to move on, not all memories are created equal, my friend.
484:{character:Joseph} Grandpa always used to say that he could sail the seven seas at peace, because he knew that he always had a harbor to come home to.
485:{character:Joseph} For me, One Han City is my harbor. Wherever I go, I know there are people waiting for me here. So there's never any need to worry, because I will always come back!
486:{character:Joseph} And don't forget—we still haven't gone to see the new "Fortunes of Adventure" film yet!
487:{character:player} What about after we do?
488:{character:Joseph} Then I'm sure we'll have something else arranged. We always will, my friend.
489:{character:player} Seems a lot of people have come. Let's go, we're the last ones.
490:{character:Joseph} Wait, my friend! Have you thought about what gift you want?
491:{character:player} Gift...? Oh, that completely slipped my mind.
492:{character:player} Surely this isn't something that the gift receiver should consider? What's up with that, Joseph? You can't think of anything to give me?
493:{character:Joseph} You'll leave it up to me to decide, yes? Hahaha! That is precisely what I wanted!
494:{character:Joseph} Because to tell you the truth, I thought about what to get you ages ago. I would like to give you... An invitation. Would you be so kind as to do me the honor of being my intrepid partner, and accompanying me on an adventure?
495:{character:player} You... Where did that suddenly come from?
496:{character:Joseph} It was very sudden. It was on that uninhabited island that the idea suddenly came to me.
497:{character:Joseph} I saw no end of novel, fascinating things while stuck on that island. Didn't you say that you wanted to see my treasures? I think that just seeing is not enough, and it's better to take you to see all the hidden marvels of nature.
498:{character:Joseph} Therefore, my friend... I want to invite you to become my adventure partner! Though I do not know if you will accept.
499:{character:player} ...You'd better make sure we don't have any strange accidents. I'm not sure I could survive months stranded in the wilderness.
500:{character:Joseph} I'll choose a route that is rookie-friendly, so don't worry about that! Let's go in then, I've got all these gifts ready, and can't wait to see their happy faces!
501:{character:player} Wait, Joseph. There's still something I want to say to you.
502:{character:player} Welcome home, Joseph.
503:{character:Joseph} ...Ha-hahaha! I'm back, {var:player_nickname}!
504:Kana Fujita
505:Wanjirou
506:Clerk
507:Santa
508:Santa?
510:{character:Joseph} Tell me about it! Seeing it makes you want to go on an adventure right away! That is "Fortunes of Adventure" for you, my friend!
511:{character:player} Eh? When did you Riichi, Kana? Crap, and I just played the tile next to the Riichi tile.
513:Joseph is dumbfounded for several seconds after "Coming Soon" appears, before slapping his thigh and leaping up from his seat, shouting and cheering.
514:{character:Joseph} Wooo! NICE! What a great night. Everything's just perfect!
515:{character:Joseph} Do you still remember what I told you before, about finding this old videotape under Grandpa's bed?
516:{character:Joseph} In the end I came up with a semi-plausible answer, which is that the movie helped him recall all the sailing adventures of his youth. Hence its title.
517:{character:Joseph} Oh, no. It's because Grandma initially thought this was some kind of romantic record of them. And she was livid when she found out the truth, and tried to throw it out. So Grandpa had to hide it under the bed!
518:{character:Joseph} Ow?! Ouch ouch... Yield! I yield!
